  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-05-02T18:08:37.109Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "So here are my feedback for the new VRChat Home. Those are purely subjective from my own experience at making worlds.\n\nBetter Colliders:\n\n- Colliders need to be generally smoother. eg: In front of the portals, the mesh collider is the same as the actual geometry and not appropriate on the floor; we can easily get stuck or bump on unwanted edges.\n\nNo Reflection?\n\n- I believe that some reflections would definitively add a nicer touch, I would add them on reflective surfaces like at the spawn below our feet on the glass/ice, also on the panels?\n\nPost-Process: \n\n- A simple color grading on neutral to get rid of the \"burned\" lightmaps and a little bit of bloom to make the lamps pops a little bit, I think this is the bare minimum for any world in general.\n\nSkybox:\n\n- I know that a skybox texture can add a lot of space itself, but this one is really pixelated and we can clearly see the banding. I would double the resolution to get a better compromise between quality and compression.\n\nUI:\n\n- The first thing that came in my mind right after the spawn: its possible to click on the pedestals from the spawn area. I can certainly imagine people changing their avatar by mistake. I would only activate the interaction with the canvas when the player is near from it.\n\nUV Scale:\n\n- I can spot many textures that have a totally different texel density (Wood floor vs the table vs rocks, etc.. ). Having a consistent texel density across all textures would probably feel more polished.",
